bound: this seat sees REWRITES and TRUNCATIONS of records it previously observed, cross-record INCOHERENCE, and — anchored on --boots — APPENDED .bootlog/.recovery growth the host's own boot count cannot account for. It still CANNOT see: a forged line-PAIR (in-progress + verdict, terminated or torn — a torn verdict rides the same in-progress attribution as a terminated one) appended into the slack of a boot the host started but fx-init never recorded (killed before its in-progress, or no bootable generation) — closing that needs a per-boot host nonce, which changes the writer's format; a coherent tamper on a store it has never observed (the enrollment gap); .bootlog lines naming gc-pruned versions (legitimate). The anchor is only as true as the host's own bookkeeping — a boot the counting host does not know about reopens the hole. An in-guest cross-check is defeated by design — that is why this seat is host-side.
